            <ArticleTitle>The Lescol Intervention Prevention Study (LIPS): start all patients on statins early after PCI.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>561-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Lescol Intervention Prevention Study (LIPS) was the first randomized trial to show a significant reduction in the risk of cardiac events in patients started on fluvastatin immediately after a successful percutaneous coronary intervention. The benefit was independent of baseline cholesterol levels. The results suggest that all patients should be discharged on lipid-lowering therapy after a percutaneous coronary intervention. Currently, this is seldom done.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
